# The production server's DIRECT dependencies (the public web app: study, trainer,
# home games, sign-in, billing). Ranges here; exact versions in server.txt.
#
# Change: edit this file, then  bash scripts/deploy_prod.sh lock  — pip resolves it ON
# the server (its Python, its platform), keeping every current pin that still fits,
# and writes server.txt. The next deploy then builds a matching environment beside
# the live one and switches to it together with the code (ops/deploy-remote.sh).
#
# torch comes from PyTorch's CPU index: the default PyPI Linux wheel pulls in
# gigabytes of CUDA libraries the server never uses.
--extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu
